1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
On Floriańska Street every bin is emptied
three times a day, full or empty.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,500
Kraków's 9,383 street bins
run on a calendar,

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:14,800
and overflowing estate shelters
push household bags onto the street.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,500
Trash Fairy is a brain for MPO
that needs no sensors.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:25,000
It collects cheap signals: a button on the bin,
reports from phones and data from drivers.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Step one:
what is overflowing right now.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,500
Step two: when each bin will cross 85%,
with city events and the weather.

8
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:42,000
Step three: tomorrow morning's route,
dozens of stops on real streets.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,500
Decisions are explicit rules in code.
AI only describes.

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,500
Now one bin, number 18,
on three devices.

11
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:00,000
A resident scans the QR code and taps "Full".
Two seconds later the bin shows "Reported".

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,500
I move the clock one hour: the bin joins the route
and the e-paper says "Crew on the way".

13
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:13,500
The driver taps "Emptied"
and the report is closed.

14
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:24,500
Residents earn points
only for reports that prove right.

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:31,500
Over four simulated weeks, empty trips
drop from 57 to 27 percent,

16
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:36,500
and shelter overflow
from 338 hours to zero.

17
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:44,500
Across Kraków:
PLN 1.5 to 2.8 million a year.

18
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Open code, synthetic data stated plainly,
hardware only where it pays off.

19
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:59,500
Kraków doesn't need more bins.
It needs a fairy.
